WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.687
Start and controls
Take a seat and press Ready. The host starts when everyone is ready. Your cards or dice are at the bottom.

00:00:12.687 --> 00:00:18.986
Follow the turn prompt. Wait for animations to finish; an expired turn is played automatically. Use Return to room after settlement.

00:00:18.986 --> 00:00:28.986
Battleship: begin with hidden fleets
Each player has a 10×10 sea. We keep our own player view; enemy ship positions have not been revealed.

00:00:28.986 --> 00:00:40.986
Goal: sink all five enemy ships
Carrier: 5 cells; battleship: 4; cruiser and submarine: 3 each; destroyer: 2. The full fleet occupies 17 cells.

00:00:40.986 --> 00:00:54.186
Choose a ship, then its bow square
Select a ship button and tap its bow square. Use Rotate, Random or Clear as needed. Select a placed ship to reposition it.

00:00:54.186 --> 00:01:04.985
Ships cannot overlap or leave the sea. Tapping the selected placed ship again rotates it. This example submits a fixed legal fleet.

00:01:04.985 --> 00:01:20.985
Confirm fleet to lock positions
All five ships must be legal before confirmation, which is final. Both players must finish before firing. Enemy readiness reveals no positions.

00:01:20.985 --> 00:01:30.885
Choose one cell in the target sea
Choose a cell you have not fired at. Mouse fires immediately; touch previews before Confirm or a second tap. This match alternates one shot each.

00:01:30.885 --> 00:01:38.985
You cannot shoot the same cell twice. Your own sea shows your ships and incoming enemy shots.

00:01:38.985 --> 00:01:54.985
Keep searching after a miss
Both first shots missed. We now choose another cell, narrowing possibilities using only public shot results.

00:01:54.985 --> 00:02:05.985
Follow a hit into neighbouring cells
We just hit a cell, but do not know the ship’s type or full length. Follow up nearby while the opponent continues taking turns.

00:02:05.985 --> 00:02:14.984
A hit does not name the ship. Only hitting every cell of that ship sinks it.

00:02:14.984 --> 00:02:28.984
A sinking reveals the ship and its cells
The battleship is now sunk, so its name and all four cells are public. Other ships still afloat remain hidden.

00:02:28.984 --> 00:02:38.884
Rule card: room options change the search
Both options are off here: ships may touch, and a hit still passes the turn.

00:02:38.884 --> 00:02:46.984
Before starting, the host can enable No touching, including diagonals, or Hit again, including sinkings. This game has no draw offers.

00:02:46.984 --> 00:03:14.984
Fast-forward through searching and sinkings
Every shot is retained at higher speed. Search from misses, hits and sinkings; enemy ships still afloat are never shown early.

00:03:14.984 --> 00:03:26.983
Resolve the final ship one cell at a time
We have sunk four ships and have one unresolved hit. Fire at its neighbour to check the remaining ship.

00:03:26.983 --> 00:03:43.967
Result: all five enemy ships sunk
We win with 41 shots, 17 hits and five sinkings. Both complete fleets become visible only after the match ends. Review the result, then return to the room.
